MID_NR20_10_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_10_m01_001: Dagdan Imperial Calendar, year 1449, Decim.\nA shocking turn of events marked the end of a year\nalready historic for its Heroic Games. Dagsion was\nquieting after months of battle when came the news.
MID_NR20_10_m01_002: Dagda the Great had woken from his long slumber\nand retaken his throne after a five-hundred-year\nabsence. He ruled the Dagdan Empire once more.
MID_NR20_10_m01_003: It should have been a joyous occasion, but not one\nfestival or celebration was held, not that day or in the\nweeks that followed. A strange waking, indeed.
MID_NR20_10_m01_004: The temples went eerily silent, which added to the\nsense of deep unease. As Dagsion entered a new\nyear, tension spread to all reaches of the city.
MID_NR20_10_m01_005: People exchanged wary glances in the streets. They\nspeculated. They shared apprehensions. And most\nof all, they waited—for any word from the temples.
MID_NR20_10_m01_006: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 1, Prologue
MID_EV20_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_000_m01_001: Are we all here? Then let's begin.
MID_EV20_000_m01_002: It has come to my attention that those barbarians of\nSaramis established a nation in my absence.
MID_EV20_000_m01_003: Meaning the loathsome bloodlines of Damascar have\nbeen despoiling imperial land for centuries.
MID_EV20_000_m01_004: I am unhappy with this state of affairs. It must end\nimmediately.
MID_EV20_000_m01_005: With respect, the Divine Sovereign himself granted\nthem that kingdom in honor of their deeds.
MID_EV20_000_m01_006: Ever since then, they've been vital to our prosperity\nas the Shield of Dagda.
MID_EV20_000_m01_007: If not for Saramis, our empire would be at constant\nwar with the ravening hordes of Southern Dagda.
MID_EV20_000_m01_008: I don't give a damn for any of that. That idiot Solel\nhad no right to make such an outrageous decision.
MID_EV20_000_m01_009: Once we conquer all of Southern Dagda for the\nempire, we'll have no need of a shield.
MID_EV20_000_m01_010: Guards, take this "loyalist" and pluck out his tongue\nfor blasphemy against the emperor!
MID_EV20_000_m01_011: What?! No, please! No!
MID_EV20_000_m01_012: Listen well. The full might of the empire and its\nvassal states shall wipe Saramis off the map.
MID_EV20_000_m01_013: March any and all associated with Saramis here to\nDagsion in chains. Young or old, I care not.
MID_EV20_000_m01_014: They'll be cast into my cauldron so that they might\natone for all their earthly sins!
MID_EV20_000_m01_015: And when that is done, we will turn our eyes to\nSouthern Dagda, which we have too long ignored.
MID_EV20_000_m01_016: We will seize control of its land and peoples by force\nuntil all of Dagda is united in me.
MID_EV20_000_m01_017: Raksha! Are my old battleships still seaworthy in\nDagsion's port?
MID_EV20_000_m01_018: They have gone unattended for some time, but with\na bit of maintenance should serve our needs.
MID_EV20_000_m01_019: Good. Put someone on it at once.
MID_EV20_000_m01_020: Hear me well, all of you. My commands are your\nsacred duty.
MID_EV20_000_m01_021: Long ago, the progenitor god Sothis charged me with\nrule over every inch of this land.
MID_EV20_000_m01_022: Our war is a noble calling in accordance with the\ngrand designs of the progenitor god!
MID_EV20_000_m01_023: I see no reason that we can't take a more merciful\napproach.
MID_EV20_000_m01_024: Perhaps disband the kingdom—relocate its subjects\nto other lands.
MID_EV20_000_m01_025: Sparing any of those worms or their vile offspring\nwas a mistake I won't repeat.
MID_EV20_000_m01_026: This time I'll compensate for my error by seeing them\nall eradicated.
MID_EV20_000_m01_027: Raksha! Issue a proclamation in my name!
MID_EV20_000_m01_028: "The Dagdan Empire will never recognize the\noccupation of its land by the barbarians of Saramis.
MID_EV20_000_m01_029: "We will soon launch a war of annihilation against\nSaramis and wipe all vestiges of them from our soil."
MID_EV20_000_m01_030: Hear me, one and all! Holy war has begun! Make\nready at once!
MID_EV20_000_m01_031: By the way...that damned Lind is still alive, isn't he?\nBring him to me now.
MID_EV20_000_m01_032: Lind?! No good can come of this...
MID_EV20_000_m01_033: I hoped never to hear that name again...
MID_EV20_000_m01_034: It's been quite a while, my grandson. Have you been\nwell? How long since we last saw each other?
MID_EV20_000_m01_035: How the hell should I know? I've been chained up\nin a pitch-black cell.
MID_EV20_000_m01_036: I quit counting the days after two hundred years,\ngive or take.
MID_EV20_000_m01_037: There wasn't anything to occupy my mind but the\npleasant thought of choking the life out of you.
MID_EV20_000_m01_038: What maniac would speak this way to the emperor?!
MID_EV20_000_m01_039: It would take twice that time to cleanse your sins\nand appease my wrath.
MID_EV20_000_m01_040: Fortunately, I have deigned to offer an opportunity.\nLind, you will oversee this campaign.
MID_EV20_000_m01_041: Do this for me and I vow to forgive your sins. You\nshall have your heart's desire.
MID_EV20_000_m01_042: Oh? My heart's desire, you say. Then I will do what\nI must.
MID_NR20_00_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_00_m01_001: Dagdan Imperial Calendar, year 1450.
MID_NR20_00_m01_002: Divine Emperor Dagda made his authority known in\nthe new year with a statement that thundered across\nthe empire: the Supreme Dagdan Declaration.
MID_NR20_00_m01_003: This far-reaching declaration reasserted that he,\nand he alone, had absolute control over the land\nas Divine Emperor.
MID_NR20_00_m01_004: Dagda revealed that Divine Sovereign Solel had\ncommitted high crimes of treason, and for that he\nhad executed Solel by his own hand.
MID_NR20_00_m01_005: The statement was also a war declaration, asserting\nthat Saramis was an unlawful occupation in the\nsouth, established contrary to his imperial will.
MID_NR20_00_m01_006: The final part of this supreme proclamation held a\nbaffling command—to demolish the Dagsion arena.\nMany citizens were put to work on this at once.
MID_NR20_00_m01_007: As dread gripped the empire, Queen Theodora rose\nto confront the growing challenge to her nation. She\nhad a decision to make—about the future of Saramis.
MID_NR20_00_m01_008: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 1, Chapter 1
MID_EV20_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_001_m01_001: Your Majesty! Something terrible has happened!\nThis is the greatest crisis in Saramis history!
MID_EV20_001_m01_002: Calm yourself, Kumos, and give your account.
MID_EV20_001_m01_003: There's news from Dagsion. The Divine Emperor is\nrevived—and he's punished the Divine Sovereign!
MID_EV20_001_m01_004: Worst of all, the Divine Emperor has declared war\non us—on Saramis!
MID_EV20_001_m01_005: Hm. I see. So the day has come.
MID_EV20_001_m01_006: This is a surprise.
MID_EV20_001_m01_007: Is it? Your tone suggests otherwise.
MID_EV20_001_m01_008: To be clear, I am surprised by Your Majesty's lack\nof surprise.
MID_EV20_001_m01_009: I have always known that this was a possibility.\nSurely the wise Bonaventure did too.
MID_EV20_001_m01_010: It is my duty to envision the worst and prepare my\npeople for it.
MID_EV20_001_m01_011: Surprise is a luxury we cannot afford now that the\ntime to act is at hand.
MID_EV20_001_m01_012: Still, I feel that it has happened far earlier than\nI anticipated.
MID_EV20_001_m01_013: Be it early or late, our resolve was steeled long ago.
MID_EV20_001_m01_014: *sigh*
MID_EV20_001_m01_015: We have no allies within the empire. And the Mosa\nare at our backs, waiting for us to show weakness.
MID_EV20_001_m01_016: Rather than await destruction, our only path is to go\non the offensive. All else wastes precious time.
MID_EV20_001_m01_017: We will bare our fangs against Dagda the Great,\nand he will feel the wrath of our ancestors!
MID_EV20_001_m01_018: It is an opportunity, in a way. Bonaventure, see that\nmy words reach the corners of the kingdom.
MID_EV20_001_m01_019: For the People of the White Egg and Damascar...\nfor all the injustice borne by our ancestors...
MID_EV20_001_m01_020: The time has come to raise the banner of revolt\nagainst the Divine Emperor and exact vengeance!
MID_EV20_001_m01_021: There is no greater cause. Your Majesty will have\nthe full support of the people.
MID_EV20_001_m01_022: Kumos, dispatch messengers to the forest peoples\nand to Troy.
MID_EV20_001_m01_023: They must put aside any grudges they may yet hold\nand make common cause with us.
MID_EV20_001_m01_024: And there is one more important task. Seek out\nwarriors of renown throughout Dagda.
MID_EV20_001_m01_025: Beseech them to ally themselves with us. This must\nbe done swiftly.
MID_EV20_001_m01_026: Whatever is available to us will be put to use. So,\nthen, what is our opening gambit?
MID_EV20_001_m01_027: We will break through the Klytius plains to the north\nand claim Agris Stronghold before they can prepare.
MID_EV20_001_m01_028: From there, we organize our forces to march on\nDagsion and slay Dagda the Great.
MID_EV20_001_m01_029: Finally...there is a weapon of last resort. Troy spoke\nof it to me long ago.
MID_EV20_001_m01_030: When you are queen, you may someday face a\nproblem truly beyond your capacity.
MID_EV20_001_m01_031: Should this happen—should Saramis's future itself be\nat risk—summon me right away.
MID_EV20_001_m01_032: I have the ability to avert calamity by calling down\na star.
MID_EV20_001_m01_033: It is a guardian star that was hung in the sky long\nago to protect you and your people.
MID_EV20_001_m01_034: A...star? What did she mean by that?
MID_EV20_001_m01_035: I do not know. But are you familiar with Lake\nBrontes in Cybele?
MID_EV20_001_m01_036: I know it is vast. And that it has a distinctive\nshape—perfectly round, as if carved by some tool.
MID_EV20_001_m01_037: Its incredible depths store an enormous volume\nof water.
MID_EV20_001_m01_038: If we could annex Cybele, we could dig canals from it\nto massively increase food production.
MID_EV20_001_m01_039: Troy claims that it is a remnant from the falling of a\nstar once in days long past.
MID_EV20_001_m01_040: Truly?! The lake is wider than the whole of Megaira.\nYou would have me believe it is artificial?
MID_EV20_001_m01_041: I have seen magical explosions—caused a few\nmyself—and it still boggles the mind.
MID_EV20_001_m01_042: I share your skepticism. But I have never known\nTroy to lie.
MID_EV20_001_m01_043: And so, if the situation calls for it, we may have a\nformidable ace up our sleeves.
MID_EV21_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV21_002_m01_001: Um... I was told that you came all the way from\nSaramis to see me?
MID_EV21_002_m01_045: 
MID_EV21_002_m01_046: 
MID_EV21_002_m01_047: 
MID_EV21_002_m01_002: I come to you with a message from Queen Theodora\nof Saramis.
MID_EV21_002_m01_003: She knows of the skill you have shown in overcoming\nmany strong foes at the Heroic Games.
MID_EV21_002_m01_004: Therefore, she asks that you put that skill to use\ndefending our kingdom!
MID_EV21_002_m01_005: Theodora is asking for me?
MID_EV21_002_m01_006: But can we join the kingdom of Saramis?
MID_EV21_002_m01_007: W-wouldn't that mean we'd make an enemy out of\nthe entire Dagdan Empire?
MID_EV21_002_m01_008: That's really scary. Could we survive that?
MID_EV21_002_m01_009: So this really is the start of a war, on a scale not seen\nin hundreds of years.
MID_EV21_002_m01_010: I'll go along with whatever you decide, Cai. I'm with\nyou no matter what.
MID_EV21_002_m01_011: Thanks, Tialla. Hmm.
MID_EV21_002_m01_012: If you would ally with us, head to Megaira.
MID_EV21_002_m01_013: Queen Theodora waits there in hopes that you will\nmeet her in person.
MID_EV21_002_m01_014: I cannot await a reply—I must hurry back\nto Saramis.
MID_EV21_002_m01_015: Then what we've heard is true.
MID_EV21_002_m01_016: Dagda the Great has revived. He killed my father,\nand he intends to invade Saramis.
MID_EV21_002_m01_017: Aurora... Are you alright? Hold it together.
MID_EV21_002_m01_018: I'm... I'm alright, Castor. But my father... We finally\ngot to talk, and now...
MID_EV21_002_m01_019: I can hardly believe it, myself. My great-grandfather\nkilled his own son, my grandpa Solel.
MID_EV21_002_m01_020: They're saying Dagda will dissolve Aurora's temple\nand...reevaluate the priesthood.
MID_EV21_002_m01_021: All because Aurora didn't respond to the Divine\nEmperor's summons.
MID_EV21_002_m01_022: My grandfather has always had a heavy-handed side.
MID_EV21_002_m01_023: But I cannot and will not stand with him.
MID_EV21_002_m01_024: It's kinda funny, the way I met Theodora. My first\nimpression was a fist to the face.
MID_EV21_002_m01_025: But now I understand she had a lot going on.\nAnd we found common ground in our battles.
MID_EV21_002_m01_026: If she's in trouble, I want to help her.
MID_EV21_002_m01_027: But will you be alright with that, Mom? Will it cause\nproblems for you?
MID_EV21_002_m01_028: Cai, I think you need to follow your heart.
MID_EV21_002_m01_029: If my mother were alive, that's what she would do.
MID_EV21_002_m01_030: Don't worry about your mom. I'll protect her.
MID_EV21_002_m01_031: Oh? In your condition? I think I'll be the one doing\nthe protecting.
MID_EV21_002_m01_032: Hehe. Just give it all you've got. No regrets, OK?
MID_EV21_002_m01_033: Naturally I'll accompany you, Cai. But what about\nyou, Peter?
MID_EV21_002_m01_034: Can't let Cai have all the fun. I'm basically his\nbrother, so he'll have to share.
MID_EV21_002_m01_035: Anyway, it might be scary, but if I don't go, I'll be\nworried about Tialla.
MID_EV21_002_m01_036: Thanks, Peter! It's always better when my friends\nare with me.
MID_EV21_002_m01_037: Aurora, with your permission, I'd like to assist\nas well.
MID_EV21_002_m01_038: I don't think you need my permission. I'm not in a\nposition to issue commands anymore.
MID_EV21_002_m01_039: But I would be very pleased to know that you'll be\nhelping Cai. Thank you, Ultand.
MID_EV21_002_m01_040: The empire will see me as a traitor.
MID_EV21_002_m01_041: I'll tell my family to leave Dagsion so they can avoid\nany possible retribution.
MID_EV21_002_m01_042: That's an excellent idea. Please direct anyone\nremaining in my temple to leave too.
MID_EV21_002_m01_043: Castor and I, though—we'll have to go into hiding.
MID_EV21_002_m01_044: Cai...please be safe. Don't overextend yourself. And\ngive my regards to Queen Theodora.
MID_EV22_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV22_002_m01_001: A message? Out with it.
MID_EV22_002_m01_025: 
MID_EV22_002_m01_026: 
MID_EV22_002_m01_027: 
MID_EV22_002_m01_002: I come to you with a message from Queen Theodora\nof Saramis.
MID_EV22_002_m01_003: She knows of the skill you have shown in overcoming\nmany strong foes at the Heroic Games.
MID_EV22_002_m01_004: Therefore, she asks that you put that skill to use\ndefending our kingdom!
MID_EV22_002_m01_005: By siding with Saramis, I will be making an\nopponent of the empire itself...
MID_EV22_002_m01_006: So it would seem. You must pray that Saramis is\nnot so easily defeated.
MID_EV22_002_m01_007: I worry that Saramis may have picked the\nwrong fight.
MID_EV22_002_m01_008: The empire is massive—and strong too. It won't go\ndown easily.
MID_EV22_002_m01_009: They don't have a choice! Dagda the Great has\nsworn to wipe them out.
MID_EV22_002_m01_010: What should they say? "Oh, sure, please kill us," and\nthen lie down and wait to die?
MID_EV22_002_m01_011: If you would ally with us, head to Megaira.
MID_EV22_002_m01_012: Queen Theodora waits there in hopes that you will\nmeet her in person.
MID_EV22_002_m01_013: I cannot await a reply—I must hurry back\nto Saramis.
MID_EV22_002_m01_014: I would cut down the emperor himself with my\nown two hands.
MID_EV22_002_m01_015: I have grown accustomed to your way of thinking,\nand this impulse comes as no surprise.
MID_EV22_002_m01_016: Having anticipated this, I am already at peace with\nit, and shall accompany you without complaint.
MID_EV22_002_m01_017: Dagda the Great has also shown something of a\nmoral deficiency, so it seems just to oppose him.
MID_EV22_002_m01_018: The unrest in Dagsion has already painted a picture\nof his barbarism.
MID_EV22_002_m01_019: And in times such as these, when we face a greater\nforce, momentum can carry the day.
MID_EV22_002_m01_020: You have me there, Fabio.
MID_EV22_002_m01_021: I'm sure it'll be OK! Where Sweetie goes, I go!
MID_EV22_002_m01_022: Well, if you're going, then I'd better go with you.
MID_EV22_002_m01_023: We'd better get a move on. Time's wasting, and we\nwant to steal a march on them.
MID_EV22_002_m01_024: Then let us go. To Megaira, the royal capital\nof Saramis!
MID_EV23_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV23_002_m01_001: It will take all our might if we hope to succeed\nagainst our foe.
MID_EV23_002_m01_002: Leave a small fragment of our troops behind. The\nbulk of them must be deployed to the front line.
MID_EV23_002_m01_003: Are we not concerned that Brezarant may invade\nSaramis behind our offensive push?
MID_EV23_002_m01_004: A fair point. Evacuate all noncombatants to Megaira\nand Fort Zanbar.
MID_EV23_002_m01_005: If the worst should happen, the defenses there should\nsuffice to maintain a stalemate.
MID_EV23_002_m01_006: If it buys us time, that is enough. We ought to raise\nour chances of success rather than focus on defense.
MID_EV23_002_m01_007: Though we must also take care not to let the Mosa\non our flank become a distraction.
MID_EV23_002_m01_008: Were they to attack from the south now, all would\nbe lost.
MID_EV23_002_m01_009: Build a militia five thousand strong as soon as you\ncan. Draft the elderly and the children if you must.
MID_EV23_002_m01_010: Give them standard equipment and send them to\nFort Zanbar to be seen by the Mosa.
MID_EV23_002_m01_011: Make it appear that we are mobilizing a large army.\nIncrease surveillance near Fort Zanbar as well.
MID_EV23_002_m01_012: But will that not provoke them all the more?
MID_EV23_002_m01_013: It is a simple show of force. Remember that the Mosa\nalso lost many in the uprising.
MID_EV23_002_m01_014: We need only appear as if we are bolstering our\ndefenses to prevent the fortress from being retaken.
MID_EV23_002_m01_015: Its defenses are such that doubling the troops there\nwill make it five times harder to capture.
MID_EV23_002_m01_016: When they see us allocate warriors there, they will\nhesitate to press the attack for some time.
MID_EV23_002_m01_017: It is vital in the upcoming campaign that they have\nno notion of the troubles facing us.
MID_EV23_002_m01_018: Sweep the palace staff for moles. Be sure that no one\nhere is secretly a Mosa agent.
MID_EV23_002_m01_019: Our borders must be closed to everyone, including\ntravelers and merchants.
MID_EV23_002_m01_020: I will make the arrangements at once.
MID_EV23_002_m01_021: So much effort. I sometimes wonder if we ought\nto have simply wiped out the Mosa.
MID_EV23_002_m01_022: It may seem like an attractive option at first blush.
MID_EV23_002_m01_023: But it would only open us to conflict with Kajimi\nand Lezeraon, whose lands are further south.
MID_EV23_002_m01_024: And if you were to conquer them as well, your realm\nwould become too vast and prone to rebellion.
MID_EV23_002_m01_025: Nations that grow unchecked cannot support their\nown weight and collapse from within.
MID_EV23_002_m01_026: This inevitability has played out many, many times\nthroughout history.
MID_EV23_002_m01_027: I see. So going further would have availed us nothing.
MID_EV23_002_m01_028: Then I shall think no more of it and turn my thoughts\nto surviving the current predicament.
MID_EV23_002_m01_029: For none of our dreams will come to anything if we\ndo not first survive this.
MID_EV24_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV24_002_m01_001: I hear you have a message for me?
MID_EV24_002_m01_040: 
MID_EV24_002_m01_041: 
MID_EV24_002_m01_042: 
MID_EV24_002_m01_043: 
MID_EV24_002_m01_002: You're a soldier from the kingdom of Saramis.\nA brave one, it would seem.
MID_EV24_002_m01_003: Granted, we're far from the center of power here,\nbut our country has declared war on yours.
MID_EV24_002_m01_004: I come to you with a message from Queen Theodora\nof Saramis.
MID_EV24_002_m01_005: She knows of the skill you have shown in overcoming\nmany strong foes at the Heroic Games.
MID_EV24_002_m01_006: Therefore, she asks that you put that skill to use\ndefending our kingdom!
MID_EV24_002_m01_007: She's assembling forces to resist the emperor?\nThat's...optimistic. And a little reckless.
MID_EV24_002_m01_008: Yes. By any estimate, their army will be dwarfed by\nthe empire's.
MID_EV24_002_m01_009: I can't muster up any reasonable scenario where\nthey triumph.
MID_EV24_002_m01_010: They have no choice but to fight back. Even if they\nfocused on defense, their doom would be certain.
MID_EV24_002_m01_011: Rather than waiting to die, Queen Theodora chooses\nto dash herself against the rocks.
MID_EV24_002_m01_012: I see a certain nobility in that.
MID_EV24_002_m01_013: If you would ally with us, head to Megaira.
MID_EV24_002_m01_014: Queen Theodora waits there in hopes that you will\nmeet her in person.
MID_EV24_002_m01_015: I cannot await a reply—I must hurry back\nto Saramis.
MID_EV24_002_m01_016: Ahh.
MID_EV24_002_m01_017: Leilidahna, are you going to support Saramis?
MID_EV24_002_m01_018: Yes... Yes, I think I will.
MID_EV24_002_m01_019: Wh-what? Have you taken leave of your senses?\nThis battle is as ill-advised as they come.
MID_EV24_002_m01_020: I told you once, and it's still true—I may be cold\nsometimes, but I'm not unfeeling.
MID_EV24_002_m01_021: Milady, do you think what happened in Kassite\nmight be coloring your judgment?
MID_EV24_002_m01_022: Maybe it is. But there's one thing I'm certain about.
MID_EV24_002_m01_023: The Dagdan Empire is on the wrong path.
MID_EV24_002_m01_024: And Dagda the Great... Something about him reeks\nlike the ditch.
MID_EV24_002_m01_025: Besides, I've fought alongside the queen before.\nI feel a certain connection with her.
MID_EV24_002_m01_028: Mu, there's no need for you to accompany me.\nGo back home.
MID_EV24_002_m01_029: What? No! That's not your choice to make. I want to\nfight with you!
MID_EV24_002_m01_030: I like you too much to let you go without me!
MID_EV24_002_m01_031: Alright. Apologies. I shouldn't have made that\ndecision on your behalf.
MID_EV24_002_m01_032: What you do here may impact Kalla's position\nin the empire.
MID_EV24_002_m01_033: Think nothing of that, Leilidahna. Do what you\nbelieve is right.
MID_EV24_002_m01_034: I...have my own doubts about the choices my\nfather is making.
MID_EV24_002_m01_035: Killing my elder brother... Now, threatening to\ndestroy Saramis. He's gone too far.
MID_EV24_002_m01_036: I'm constrained from doing anything openly, but you\ncan be my eyes and ears.
MID_EV24_002_m01_037: There's little I can do to support you, I'm afraid.
MID_EV24_002_m01_038: So I would urge abundant caution.
MID_EV24_002_m01_039: It's encouraging enough to know your heart is with\nus. Thank you, Kalla.
