MID_NR20_01_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_01_m01_001: Dagdan Imperial Calendar, year 1450, Janai.
MID_NR20_01_m01_002: Queen Theodora set off with her grand army and\nmarched as if a fierce wind was at their backs, soon\ngoing north, deeper into the Dagdan Empire.
MID_NR20_01_m01_003: Theodora's scouts caught sight of the imperial army\nlate one evening in Callisto county, which was the\ngoddess Aurora's domain.
MID_NR20_01_m01_004: The queen's army made camp at the Klytius plains\nwith intent to strike them decisively at dawn.
MID_NR20_01_m01_005: But a combined force was gathering to their\nnorth—unknown to them—drawing in more legions,\nboth from the empire and Arago.
MID_NR20_01_m01_006: And the Brezarant army, coming from the southwest,\ntook a position in the hills above the plains.
MID_NR20_01_m01_007: Theodora's army was caught in a predicament.
MID_NR20_01_m01_008: They were surrounded by the enemy, tensions rising\nin the night, and could do nothing about it except\nwait for the battle to come at morning's first light.
MID_NR20_01_m01_009: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 1, Chapter 3
MID_EV20_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_004_m01_001: I am pleased with our march thus far. You are all\ndoing well.
MID_EV20_004_m01_002: Our battle begins at sunrise. See that the soldiers\nrest well tonight.
MID_EV20_004_m01_003: But do not let them grow complacent. A night raid\ncould be disastrous.
MID_EV20_004_m01_004: Will do, boss! Wouldn't wanna stumble now after we\nworked so hard to get here.
MID_EV20_004_m01_005: Looks like I found you, Theodora. I got your\nmessage, so here I am.
MID_EV20_004_m01_006: Cai! It is good of you to come in our hour of need.
MID_EV20_004_m01_007: You proved your strength against me, after all.\nBut are you certain you wish to join our cause?
MID_EV20_004_m01_008: I'm sure. And don't worry about my mom. She's put\nsome distance between herself and her temple.
MID_EV20_004_m01_009: Anyway, I know you're on the right side. That's\nwhy I'm here.
MID_EV20_004_m01_010: Mom sends her regards, by the way. And she wants\nall of us to stay safe.
MID_EV20_004_m01_011: I see. Thank you, Cai. I shall do what I can, both for\nyour sake and for Aurora's.
MID_EV20_004_m01_012: I'll get set up. Let's give this our best shot, Theodora.
MID_EV20_004_m01_013: So this is where you make camp, Theodora.
MID_EV20_004_m01_014: Dietrich? This is a surprise. I was not expecting you\nto extend a hand.
MID_EV20_004_m01_015: It is not you I have come for.
MID_EV20_004_m01_016: I wish to face the strongest opponents. That is all.
MID_EV20_004_m01_017: There is a veiled insult in your alliance. Nevertheless,\nI am grateful for your aid.
MID_EV20_004_m01_018: In truth, I would not turn away any allies now.
MID_EV20_004_m01_019: The battle is to begin at dawn, yes? If so, I will\ntake my rest.
MID_EV20_004_m01_020: Your Majesty, is it wise to harbor such a man in\nour camp?
MID_EV20_004_m01_021: Wise? Who can say. Of all our allies, he is the one\nwho bears watching most.
MID_EV20_004_m01_022: But if he is true to his word, I am reassured to have\nhim on our side.
MID_EV20_004_m01_023: Good evening, Queen Theodora. We're settling in\nwell so far.
MID_EV20_004_m01_024: Leda! Well met. This is a surprise.
MID_EV20_004_m01_025: A surprise? I could easily be offended, Your Majesty.\nYou did summon me.
MID_EV20_004_m01_026: True enough, and you have my apologies. But are\nyou certain of this? Our task is not simple.
MID_EV20_004_m01_027: One could say it would be wiser to have ignored the\nsummons. But I'm not the biggest fan of the empire.
MID_EV20_004_m01_028: Whatever your reasons, it is comforting to count\nyou among our allies.
MID_EV20_004_m01_029: The battle will begin at sunrise. You ought to rest\nand recoup your strength until then.
MID_EV20_004_m01_030: But first, dinner will be served shortly. I hope you\nwill partake.
MID_EV20_004_m01_031: Hehe. I have a growing young girl with me who I'm\nsure will appreciate the meal. See you at dinner.
MID_EV20_004_m01_086: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_032: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_033: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_034: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_035: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_036: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_037: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_038: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_039: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_040: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_041: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_042: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_043: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_044: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_045: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_046: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_047: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_048: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_049: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_050: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_004_m01_053: Dagda's vassals moved more quickly than\nI had hoped.
MID_EV20_004_m01_054: I knew they would act, of course, but we are facing\none of the worst-case scenarios.
MID_EV20_004_m01_055: Yeah. It woulda been great to be past here by the\ntime Brezarant's crew showed up.
MID_EV20_004_m01_056: It's weird for us all to run into each other on the\nsame day like it was planned.
MID_EV20_004_m01_057: Ah, but Brezarant's forces are focused on us and not\nSaramis itself.
MID_EV20_004_m01_058: I would count that as a victory.
MID_EV20_004_m01_059: They say that land has been mired in chaos since\nthe previous king died without a successor.
MID_EV20_004_m01_060: I was hoping that state of affairs would continue, but\nI gather they have anointed a new king.
MID_EV20_004_m01_061: To march a large force through the Mulciber\nMarshlands is no mean feat.
MID_EV20_004_m01_062: This new king of theirs must be an inspiring leader.
MID_EV20_004_m01_063: Hm. Knowing that, we shall need to brace ourselves\nfor a bloody engagement.
MID_EV20_004_m01_064: Huh?
MID_EV20_004_m01_065: Sniper! Boss, they're hitting us at night!
MID_EV20_004_m01_066: Hold your positions! If this was a true assault, they\nwould have let loose a volley.
MID_EV20_004_m01_067: A single burning arrow is meant to draw our gaze.\nAnd see here—a letter is attached.
MID_EV20_004_m01_068: Uch. Writing. I can make head nor tail of it.
MID_EV20_004_m01_069: Tell me what it says, Bonaventure. You can\nread, yes?
MID_EV20_004_m01_070: I can, to some extent. How did you know,\nYour Majesty?
MID_EV20_004_m01_071: I always believed it impossible you could stay so\nwell-informed solely through the oral tradition.
MID_EV20_004_m01_072: In other circumstances, I would see you flogged for it.\nNow, though, it is our saving grace.
MID_EV20_004_m01_073: On those grounds, I shall withhold punishment\njust the once.
MID_EV20_004_m01_074: Hoho. I am glad for this letter then.
MID_EV20_004_m01_075: What does it say? Hurry up and read it to me.
MID_EV20_004_m01_076: One moment... I'm a bit out of practice, alas.
MID_EV20_004_m01_077: Hrm? Oh my... What?!
MID_EV20_004_m01_078: Out with it, Bonaventure! What does the letter say?
MID_EV20_004_m01_079: I have incredible news, Your Majesty.
MID_EV20_004_m01_080: The kingdom of Brezarant is... Unbelievable. I dare\nsay the heavens are on our side.
MID_EV20_004_m01_081: Bonaventure, adjust the plans accordingly.
MID_EV20_004_m01_082: As you wish!
MID_EV20_004_m01_083: Tobias, gather our commanders for an emergency\nmeeting. Slap them awake if you must.
MID_EV20_004_m01_084: On it, boss!
MID_EV20_004_m01_085: We can win this battle. I know it. But we now have\nmuch to do before dawn breaks.
MID_EV20_005_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_005_m01_017: 
MID_EV20_005_m01_018: 
MID_EV20_005_m01_019: 
MID_EV20_005_m01_021: 
MID_EV20_005_m01_022: 
MID_EV20_005_m01_001: Proud warriors of Saramis, turn your ears to me now.
MID_EV20_005_m01_002: And those of you who heeded my call and gathered\nin response—hear me now!
MID_EV20_005_m01_003: I swear to you that we will seize victory in this\nunjust war.
MID_EV20_005_m01_004: For the sake of our mother—the benevolent goddess\nYu Phas, cruelly murdered by Dagda the Great.
MID_EV20_005_m01_005: And to avenge Damascar, our ancestors who, like us,\nwere persecuted without cause!
MID_EV20_005_m01_006: We of Saramis carry the honor they passed down\nto us.
MID_EV20_005_m01_007: We fight now for the sake of the children to come,\nwhose faces are as yet unknown.
MID_EV20_005_m01_008: We WILL march on Dagsion and drive the stake of\nour wrath into the Divine Emperor!
MID_EV20_005_m01_009: The curtain shall rise on that tale with our battle\nat Klytius this morning.
MID_EV20_005_m01_010: Today, I ask you to put your lives in my hands!
MID_EV20_005_m01_011: In return, I promise to deliver you a complete and\ntotal victory!
MID_EV20_005_m01_012: We shall pound the fear of us into the very marrow\nof their bones!
MID_EV20_005_m01_013: We shall show them how Saramis fights, and they\nwill remember it as a day of catastrophe!
MID_EV20_005_m01_014: Our mother goddess, who watches over us from\nthe heavens...
MID_EV20_005_m01_015: Bring us victory this day! We offer our souls and\ndedicate this fight to Yu Phas!
MID_EV20_005_m01_016: We offer our souls and dedicate this fight to Yu Phas!
MID_EV20_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_031_m01_001: There's news, sir! Our troops have suffered heavy\ncasualties!
MID_EV20_031_m01_002: The Saramis army that appeared from our flank is\nlaying waste to our vanguard.
MID_EV20_031_m01_003: The worst losses are the troops we deployed to the\nfront line. We're headed for a rout!
MID_EV20_031_m01_004: Oh? That sly vixen. It's a very brazen trick\nshe's pulled.
MID_EV20_031_m01_005: This isn't how it was supposed to go! Wasn't our\narmy meant to enjoy an overwhelming victory?!
MID_EV20_031_m01_006: And why hasn't Brezarant sent their forces to\nsupport us? What are they waiting for?!
MID_EV20_031_m01_007: Don't tell me they plan to show up late and steal\nall the glory!
MID_EV20_031_m01_008: Believe you me, General, Dagda the Great will hear\nall about this!
MID_EV20_031_m01_009: Whatever makes you happy.
MID_EV20_031_m01_010: The damnable muscle-headed Brezarant barbarians\nbetter brace themselves for a scolding!
MID_EV20_031_m01_011: Let's hope their reasons for staying put are as shallow\nas you say. I have an uneasy feeling about this.
MID_EV20_031_m01_012: More news, sir! The Brezarant army is on the move.
MID_EV20_031_m01_013: They're charging down the hill as fast as they can!
MID_EV20_031_m01_014: Ha. It's about time those useless layabouts stopped\nsitting around.
MID_EV20_031_m01_015: Terrible news, sir! Brezarant's on the march,\nalright...
MID_EV20_031_m01_016: and they're going the wrong way! They're not\nheaded for Saramis at all!
MID_EV20_031_m01_017: They're circling around the vanguard and charging\nat us from the side!
MID_EV20_031_m01_018: They're poised to strike at our main force!
MID_EV20_031_m01_019: WH-WH-WHAT?!
MID_EV20_031_m01_020: Alright. So that's how it's going to be.
MID_EV20_031_m01_021: {SetColor=Gray}Mars, you bastard. So this is your answer...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV20_006_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_006_m01_089: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_090: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_091: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_092: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_093: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_001: Victory is ours! Cry triumph to the heavens!
MID_EV20_006_m01_002: Your Majesty, the new king of Brezarant has arrived!
MID_EV20_006_m01_003: So he took the initiative, did he? I shall grant him\nhis audience. Let him through.
MID_EV20_006_m01_004: Theodora, it's been some time. I have to commend\nyou for your leadership in that battle.
MID_EV20_006_m01_005: Bertrand! This is a big surprise!
MID_EV20_006_m01_006: Cai? Yours is not a face I thought I'd see today.
MID_EV20_006_m01_007: Did you get your wish after the Heroic Games?
MID_EV20_006_m01_008: Yeah. Fortunately things worked out. Pop's living\nwith Mom now.
MID_EV20_006_m01_009: Then why leave them? War has a way of tearing\nchildren from their parents.
MID_EV20_006_m01_010: I've made up my mind. And my parents said I should\ndo what I think is best.
MID_EV20_006_m01_011: Plus, I'm glad I get to fight alongside you like this\nagain, Bertrand!
MID_EV20_006_m01_012: The White-Maned Demon... We meet again.
MID_EV20_006_m01_013: I had hoped for another chance to duel.
MID_EV20_006_m01_014: I'd be more than happy to accept your challenge.\nAt a later date, perhaps?
MID_EV20_006_m01_015: I think we may want to finish our foes before we\nstart killing each other.
MID_EV20_006_m01_016: For now, that is true. But you must not die in\nthis battle.
MID_EV20_006_m01_017: That alone will make it worth raising my blade\nthis day.
MID_EV20_006_m01_018: Hmm. You don't seem like quite the same man\nI remember.
MID_EV20_006_m01_019: Of late, my companions have said much the same.\nI myself do not know.
MID_EV20_006_m01_020: Bertrand. To run into you here of all places.
MID_EV20_006_m01_021: Guillermo's daughter. You've thrown in with us\nas well?
MID_EV20_006_m01_022: I'd planned to take your life after our invasion\nreached Dagsion.
MID_EV20_006_m01_023: But that's not how things shook out.
MID_EV20_006_m01_024: Instead...I'll just have to take my chance here.
MID_EV20_006_m01_025: I'm sorry, but I'd ask you to set your vendetta\naside until the war's behind us.
MID_EV20_006_m01_026: I now recall that the two of you share some\nsordid history.
MID_EV20_006_m01_027: But the White-Maned Demon is right. Can this not\nwait until the matter at hand is resolved?
MID_EV20_006_m01_028: Very well. But Bertrand, do not flee. Do not die.\nNot before I get my revenge.
MID_EV20_006_m01_029: The White-Maned Demon. Thank you for your aid.\nWith your assistance, we achieved a great victory.
MID_EV20_006_m01_030: I always believed we could win, but I had braced\nmyself to pay for it with heavy casualties.
MID_EV20_006_m01_031: We owe it to Brezarant that our losses were far\nlower than anticipated.
MID_EV20_006_m01_032: Imagine my surprise to find that the man I crossed\nblades with has become a king.
MID_EV20_006_m01_033: It goes against my nature, but I cannot help but feel\nfate's hand at work here.
MID_EV20_006_m01_034: Probably so. I don't see how anything less could have\nled to a meeting like this.
MID_EV20_006_m01_035: Now we stake our two nations' futures on the\noutcome of this war.
MID_EV20_006_m01_036: Yes. Though given the choice, I would rather not\ngamble with such things.
MID_EV20_006_m01_079: The White-Maned Demon. Thank you for your aid.\nWith your assistance, we achieved a great victory.
MID_EV20_006_m01_080: I always believed we could win, but I had braced\nmyself to pay for it with heavy casualties.
MID_EV20_006_m01_081: We owe it to Brezarant that our losses were far\nlower than anticipated.
MID_EV20_006_m01_082: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_083: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_084: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_085: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_086: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_037: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_038: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_039: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_040: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_041: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_042: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_043: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_044: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_045: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_046: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_047: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_048: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_049: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_050: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_006_m01_052: The reunions can come later. Let us speak of the\nwork before us.
MID_EV20_006_m01_053: Tell me of the Brezarant forces you have brought\nwith you.
MID_EV20_006_m01_054: I led half my country's army here, around 35\nthousand strong.
MID_EV20_006_m01_055: These troops will march with yours in the press\ntoward Dagsion.
MID_EV20_006_m01_056: But in declaring revolt on the empire, I know I'm\nstarting a blaze I can't snuff out.
MID_EV20_006_m01_057: Now that the fire is set, we ought to discuss what\nDagda will look like after this war.
MID_EV20_006_m01_058: Very well. I will arrange a space where we might\nconfer. I would like to hear your true intentions.
MID_EV20_006_m01_059: I have many other questions to ask you besides.\nThis calls for the special supply of ghosh.
MID_EV20_006_m01_060: I am eager to learn from you how things reached\nthis point.
MID_EV20_006_m01_061: So you officially completed the Trial of the Chariot.\nThe prisoner has become a king.
MID_EV20_006_m01_062: Ah, well. You would never have been satisfied as\na member of my entourage.
MID_EV20_006_m01_063: The arena tested me. I bled, I broke, I suffered.
MID_EV20_006_m01_064: But nothing compared to the horrors of Cydonia—\nor what I saw beneath Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV20_006_m01_065: This world is rife with injustice. Not that that's news\nto a child of Damascar.
MID_EV20_006_m01_066: When the crown fell on my head, I thought...perhaps\nwe can end it. Perhaps we can stop the suffering.
MID_EV20_006_m01_067: The emperor had other ideas. Now I think achieving\nthe world I want means allying with you.
MID_EV20_006_m01_068: Hm. I find your naïve optimism charming in its way.
MID_EV20_006_m01_069: But I was under the impression that Mars, the\nBringer of War, held sway over Brezarant.
MID_EV20_006_m01_070: Did he give you leave to turn your blades against\nthe Divine Emperor?
MID_EV20_006_m01_071: The Bringer of War doesn't much trust the\nDivine Emperor.
MID_EV20_006_m01_072: You might say he's putting the question to\nthe heavens.
MID_EV20_006_m01_073: Ah. He believes the matter of justice will be settled\nby strength. How very like him.
MID_EV20_006_m01_074: I'm not saying that his code starts and ends at\nstrength in battle.
MID_EV20_006_m01_075: In fact, it seemed to me that Mars was already\nplanning to take up arms against his father.
MID_EV20_006_m01_076: I see. Knowing that, I am comfortable putting my\ntrust in you.
MID_EV20_006_m01_077: Let us form an official pact. From now on, we are\nthe Saramis-Brezarant Alliance.
MID_EV20_006_m01_078: We shall march on Dagsion to slay Dagda the Great.\nFor he has left us no other choice.
MID_NR20_07_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_07_m01_001: Theodora and Bertrand...
MID_NR20_07_m01_002: Young monarchs, united by oath. Their alliance now\nbound their kingdoms in purpose—joining their\nconviction and confidence.
MID_NR20_07_m01_003: The alliance merged their troops into an army of\ngreat size. The Saramis-Brezarant Alliance was\nover one hundred thousand soldiers strong.
MID_NR20_07_m01_004: As news of their historic victory at Klytius spread\nthrough Dagda and to the city at its heart, the\nwhole of the empire seemed to tremble.
MID_NR20_07_m01_005: The Alliance, spurred by triumph, marched on to\nAmalthea. They planned to breach the border at\nAgris Stronghold, and soon after storm Dagsion.
MID_NR20_07_m01_006: But their momentum came at an unexpected cost.\nThe Alliance, which had grown so suddenly,\nwould face a perilous threat—from within.
MID_NR20_07_m01_007: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 1, Chapter 3